From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taher Chegini <cheginit@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:13:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix(kernel): make the Muskingum-Cunge kernel
 deterministic

secant2_h read Qj and C1..C4 on entry while declaring them intent(out), so the
compiler dropped the caller's stores and the reads took stack residue. Forward
and reverse passes over 46,080 cases disagreed on 8,349; now on none.

Ported to CIROH-UA/t-route d29f663 from NGWPC/t-route commit 2bd0c0c2
(PR #123, merged 2026-08-21). NGWPC's kernel had a performance refactor
(7c9153ff) before this commit, so the hunk context differs; the change itself
is the same: Qj_0 = 0 at label 110 as in WRF-Hydro's SUBMUSKINGCUNGE, the
intent(inout) actuals defined before first use, and Qj, C1..C4 intent(inout).
Brodie Alexander reported the C1..C4 read and made the same correction in
CIROH-UA/rs_route#7 (2026-03-30).

Co-authored-by: Brodie Alexander <baalexander2@crimson.ua.edu>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90  | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90 b/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90
index 5847448..ff49872 100644
--- a/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90
+++ b/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90
@@ -74,6 +74,16 @@ subroutine muskingcungenwm(dt, qup, quc, qdp, ql, dx, bw, tw, twcc,&
         .or. qdp .gt. 0.0_prec .or. qdc .gt. 0.0_prec) then  !only solve if there's water to flux
 110 continue
 
+        !* Qj_0 = 0 is the reference's (MUSKINGCUNGE.f90 label 110), lost in the
+        !* port; interval 1 forms X from it on the first pass. The rest are here
+        !* so every intent(inout) actual is defined before its first use.
+        Qj_0 = 0.0_prec
+        Qj   = 0.0_prec
+        C1   = 0.0_prec
+        C2   = 0.0_prec
+        C3   = 0.0_prec
+        C4   = 0.0_prec
+
         !Uncomment next two lines for old initialization
         !WPC = 0.0_prec
         !AREAC = 0.0_prec
@@ -204,7 +214,12 @@ subroutine secant2_h(z, bw, bfd, twcc, s0, n, ncc, dt, dx, &
     real(prec), intent(in) :: dt, dx
     real(prec), intent(in) :: qdp, ql, qup, quc
     real(prec), intent(in) :: h
-    real(prec), intent(out) :: Qj, C1, C2, C3, C4, X
+    !* NOT intent(out): interval 1 reads Qj, and interval 2 reads C1..C4, before
+    !* assigning them. Declaring them intent(out) let the compiler treat the
+    !* caller's stores as dead and delete them, so the reads picked up whatever
+    !* the stack held and the published depth depended on call order.
+    real(prec), intent(inout) :: Qj, C1, C2, C3, C4
+    real(prec), intent(out) :: X
     integer,    intent(in) :: interval
 
     real(prec) :: twl, AREA, WP, R
